# What this is: the list of every Blender start of the gravel trial (12 of the 12 allowed): run number, picture size, what it was for, clock time. Written by hand as each run started.
run 1 | 512 dots | first look: layout debug views, finished colour, layer pictures | 09:24
run 2 | 512 dots | turned grids, FACETS layer, colour and soil changes | 09:29
run 3 | 640 dots | brighter soil, darker stones, rust through the tint settings; colour and height; two seed sets | 09:33
run 4 | 1254 dots | first full-size probe (colour + height) to see the like-for-like score | 09:38
run 5 | 640 dots | ragged stone edges, subtler facets, more patchy stone paint, bigger rust clumps | 09:44
run 6 | 1254 dots | probe 2: ragged edges, orange top tone, MOSS out of the stack; colour + three height versions (rule, real relief, COMBINE's own rule) | 09:48
run 7 | 1254 dots | probe 3: calmer soil crumbs, darker soil, less big-patch variation, height blend 0.9; colour + height | 09:58
run 8 | 1254 dots | probe 4: back to the round 6 crumbs and grain, darker soil colours kept, more pale lumps, brighter lit faces; colour + height | 10:03
run 9 | 1254 dots | probe 5: no paint tongues (fade_direction 0) to remove the comb-like teeth on stone tops; colour + height | 10:09
run 10 | 1254 dots | the final bake: three seed sets (colour, 16-bit height, roughness, metallic) and the height with COMBINE's own rule for seed set 1 | 10:13
run 11 | 512, 627, 320 dots | the proof tests: half-tile shift (1 and 2 tiles across), layer masks, independence (Amount 0 and Seed + 1), node counts | 10:28
run 12 | 1254 dots | the 'what each layer adds' ladder: four partial stacks (colour only; + outline; + damage; + facets), colour and height | 10:43
